WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Take a single neutron out of a nucleus
and leave it completely on its own.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.520
It does not last.

3
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:10.490
It decays, and three
particles emerge: a proton,

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.410
an electron and an antineutrino.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.760
The same kind of change
happens inside nuclei.

6
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.220
It is called beta-minus decay.

7
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.650
So what actually changes inside
the neutron when it decays?

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.100
In this mission, you'll find out which
of the four interactions is behind beta

9
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.030
decay.

10
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.840
Then you'll run beta-plus decay, where a
proton inside a nucleus becomes a neutron.

11
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: find out what
changes inside a decaying neutron.
